{
  "version": "1.15.15",
  "channel": "stable",
  "notes": "- The **Rollback snapshots** card lists the saved snapshots again. A display\n  that had taken three or more of them -- by now, every display -- showed\n  \"None yet\" even though the snapshots were there and an undo would have\n  worked: the page was cutting the list off before it could be read. The\n  snapshots themselves were never touched, and a rollback still worked from\n  the command line the whole time; this only restores the page's view of them.\n- The **Screen rotation** setting now uses the same words as Windows --\n  **Landscape**, **Portrait**, **Landscape (flipped)**, **Portrait (flipped)**\n  -- instead of \"90 left / 90 right\". It matches what the same panel was set to\n  under Windows, so there is nothing to translate. Nothing about how a display\n  rotates changed; only the labels.\n- **Machines converted from Windows now come up on whatever Wi-Fi they were on,\n  open networks included.** The installer keeps the exact connection it used to\n  reach the network rather than assuming a WPA2 password -- so an open network,\n  or a WPA3 one, is no longer left unable to rejoin the network it was installed\n  over. (This is in the installer, so it applies to new conversions, not to a\n  display that is already running.)",
  "notes_covers": ["1.15.14", "1.15.15"],
